Since binutils 2.31 the generic .nop [size] pseudo-op shadows the SPU nop
instruction, as NO_PSEUDO_DOT is set. GCC emits "nop 127" (RT=$127) which
then expands to 127 bytes of nops, breaking hbrr branch hint distances:

  Error: Relocation doesn't fit. (relocation value = 0x518)

Force nop to be an instruction, like set and eqv.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/gas/config/tc-spu.c	2026-11-19 16:45:30.249312036 +0100
+++ b/gas/config/tc-spu.c	2026-11-19 16:45:30.258735647 +0100
@@ -101,6 +101,9 @@ const pseudo_typeS md_pseudo_table[] =
   /* Likewise for eqv.  */
   {"eqv", NULL, 0},
   {".eqv", s_set, -1},
+  /* Likewise for nop, nop with operand is not a fill count.  */
+  {"nop", NULL, 0},
+  {".nop", s_nop, 0},
   {0,0,0}
 };
 
